/**
 * @mainpage Daniyal Machine Learning Framework (DMLFW)
 *
 * @section about About This Project
 *
 * The Daniyal Machine Learning Framework (DMLFW) is a personal, educational project
 * designed to deepen understanding of machine learning by implementing its foundations
 * from scratch in C.
 *
 * The primary focus is clarity, simplicity, and learning rather than production-level performance.
 * DMLFW serves as a toolkit and journal for experimenting with core ML concepts.
 *
 * @section features Features
 *
 * - Core data structures: vectors, matrices, and lists (supporting double and string data types).  
 * - Mathematical utilities for basic algebra, statistics, and transformations.  
 * - Machine learning algorithms: batch, stochastic, and mini-batch gradient descent implementations.  
 * - Data preprocessing utilities: encoding, normalization, and scaling.  
 * - Model evaluation metrics such as R² score and accuracy.  
 * - Centralized error handling and general file/string utilities.  
 *
 * @section usage Usage
 *
 * The framework is distributed as source code. Build with a standard C compiler.
 * Include framework headers and link against the static library.
 * Examples and tools provide practical usage demos.
 *
 * @section structure Project Structure
 *
 * - ml-framework: Core framework modules including data structures and ML algorithms.  
 * - ml-examples: Example programs demonstrating ML workflows.  
 * - tools: Command-line tools for dataset preprocessing and encoding.  
 *
 * @section documentation Documentation
 *
 * Detailed API references are available in this generated documentation.
 *
 * @section contributions Contributions
 *
 * Contributions to improve clarity, add examples, or extend educational coverage are welcome.
 * Please open an issue or contact the maintainer before submitting pull requests.
 *
 * @section contact Contact
 *
 * Maintainer: Mohammed Daniyal  
 * Email: mohammeddaniyal453@gmail.com  
 * LinkedIn: <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/mohammeddaniyalali">mohammeddaniyalali</a>
 *
 * @section acknowledgments Acknowledgments
 *
 * Special thanks to mentor Prafull Kelkar Sir for invaluable guidance and support.
 */
